// MP, XP, GP and TP resonance decay steering
// alpha_ls and helicity are relative complex angular parameters
// The physical helicity tensor is normalized to sum |H|^2 = 1
// BR and width fix the absolute decay coupling unless g_decay_TP specifies a TP value

// Particles are identified by their PDG IDs
// Add new particles and branchings here as you wish
//
//                / daughter 1
//               /
//  mother -----x----- daughter N
//               \
//                \ daughter 2
//
// 2-body helicity decay amplitude format:
// 
// - "[PDG1,PDG2,...]": compact signed daughter PDG key
// - "BR":         branching ratio for the specified charge channel
// - "basis":      "alpha_ls" or "helicity"; selects which coupling basis block is active
// - "alpha_ls":   relative LS amplitudes [l,s,magnitude,phase [rad]]
// - "helicity":   relative helicity amplitudes [lambda1,lambda2,magnitude,phase [rad]]
// - "zeta":       MP, XP, GP and TP decay phases [rad], applied with exp(1j*zeta)
// - "CP":         [C_symmetry, P_symmetry] flags charge-conjugation and parity conservation
// - "FF_decay":   Decay vertex form factor
// - "g_decay_TP": Tensor Pomeron model decay couplings

// l is the relative angular momentum of daughters in the mother rest frame
// s = |s1 - s2|, |s1 - s2| + 1, ..., s1 + s2 is the 'total spin' of daughters
// |l - s| <= J <= l + s
// 
// l = 0  S-wave
// l = 1  P-wave
// l = 2  D-wave
// l = 3  F-wave
// l = 4  G-wave
// l = 5  H-wave
// l = 6  I-wave
// 
// Spectroscopic notation ^{2s+1}L_J:
// s = total spin of daughters
// L = S, P, D, F, ... from l
// J = mother spin

// BR values collected manually from PDGlive; BR = Gamma_partial / Gamma
//
// Example of isospin and PDG notation:
//
// Gamma(X -> \pi+\pi-) = 2 x Gamma(X -> \pi0 \pi0) = 2/3 Gamma(X -> \pi\pi)
// Gamma(X -> K+K-)     = Gamma(X -> K0\bar{K0})    = 1/2 Gamma(X -> K\bar{K})
// 
// X above having isospin I = 0, ratios obtained with CG SU(2)-coefficients
//
// The channel key identifies the daughters in the stored leg order
//
// (c) 2026 Mikael Mieskolainen
// Licensed under the MIT License <http://opensource.org/licenses/MIT>.

